  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve Secondary Teachers Education in the National Teachers&apos; Colleges (NTC) (of Mubende and Kabale)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- The College&apos;s students, education managers and academic staff of NTC Mubende and Kabale
- The Ministry of Education, Sciences, Technology and Sports - in particular the teachers and instructors Education and Training departement (TIET).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased access to quality post-primary education and training as a part of Universal Post-Primary Education and Training (UPPET) Improved teaching and practice-oriented learning environment sustained by strengthened management. 1: The organisational and financial management capacity of NTC Muni to deliver its strategic priorities is strenghtened.
2: Access to quality training and learning facilities in NTC Muni is increased
3: The capacity of CMU and PDU to deliver their services in a timely, efficient and effective way is strengthened</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention aims to improve the quality of education and training of future teachers in National Teachers Colleges (NTCs), pursuing three activities: pedagogic support (ATL - Active Teaching and Learning); strengthening the management capacities of NTCs; and rehabilitation of infrastructure and installations (in the NTCs of Mubende and Kabale - two of five secondary teachers training colleges in Uganda funded by the Government through the Ministry of Education and Sports). The extension of the project under the Bridging Programme emphasizes the digital transition in education to develop a &apos;hybrid education&apos;, elaborating among others digital tools for all five NTC&apos;s. The intervention will improve the training of secondary teacher trainers in National Teachers&#x2019; College Mubende and Kabale (one of the five secondary school teacher training colleges in Uganda funded by the Government through the Ministry of Education and Sports),focusing both on small infrastructure/equipment, institutional development and pedagogical methods (ATL - Active Teaching and Learning).   The project aims to contribute to improved quality of post primary education and training in NTCs Mubende and Kabale, as part of the Universal Post-Primary Education and Training (UPPET) as well as produce competent teachers through effective use of acquired management and pedagogical competencies and proper use of infrastructure and facilities. The Improve Secondary Teachers Education project is a Ugandan initiative focused on teacher training within the National Teachers&apos; Colleges (NTC) of Mubende and Kabale. Aligned with the Universal Post-Primary Education and Training (UPPET), the project aims to enhance the quality of post-primary education and produce competent teachers by effectively utilizing acquired management and pedagogical skills, as well as optimizing infrastructure and facilities. The project is financed by the BTC Operations Fund and feasibility studies, with implementation overseen by Enabel. The intervention encompasses three results: the elaboration and completion of NTCs&#x2019; Strategic Plans, further development and partial implementation of an infrastructure master plan, and support for the professional development of teacher trainers, teachers, and education managers. This project is coordinated with other sector interventions of the Belgian Development Cooperation and other stakeholders, ensuring a complementary and synergistic approach within the education sector. The intervention is also aligned with relevant strategic plans of the Government of Uganda at both national/sector and NTC levels, promoting the digital agenda and integrating cross-cutting themes such as environment, gender, and HIV/AIDS where feasible.</narrative>
  </description>
